  "readmeFile": "ReadmeNuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Runtime:\n- New app setting WritePermissionDeniedBehavior (ViewOnly / Disabled) chooses how a module or field is shown when the current user has no write permission (UserWriteCondition / DataWriteCondition / PermissionField write condition). ViewOnly keeps the read-only display (default, unchanged). Disabled keeps the input controls and disables them instead. Read-only by design (CanCreate / CanUpdate = false) is not affected.\nLicense:\n- Fixed: a Client license was reported as invalid in WPF / WinForms client-server apps (the license banner was shown). It is now accepted there; it is still rejected on the designer and on web servers.\n- WinForms apps are now recognized as a desktop client even when the license is checked before Application.Run (the entry assembly's references are inspected in addition to the running Application).\nBlazor Hybrid (WPF / WinForms / MAUI):\n- Fixed: the process could terminate right after a page was shown with \"Cannot read properties of null (reading 'setAttribute')\" from FocusControl.js when the module was re-rendered while the focus control was being attached. The attach is now skipped in that case.",
